@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Host-local provider configuration
+
+A plain provider may set `privateConfig` to an absolute YAML path or a path
+starting with `~/`. The provider's ordinary protocol URLs remain logical bases;
+the private file replaces their destinations at signing time. Only the file
+reference is serialized. Credentials and destinations are not copied into
+providers.json, GUI payloads, sync or source control. The file must be regular,
+at most 1 MiB and owner-only on Unix. Unknown fields, missing files and malformed
+files fail closed. Windows owners must enforce equivalent ACLs themselves.
+
+```yaml
+bearer: REPLACE_LOCALLY
+headers:
+  X-Source: local-tag
+endpoints:
+  chat: https://api.example.invalid/external
+  responses: https://api.example.invalid/external
+  anthropic: https://api.example.invalid/messages-api
+normalize_errors: true
+model_apis:
+  - prefix: alternate-
+    protocol: chat
+exclude_models: []
+```
+
+Each endpoint is a base before its protocol's usual suffix. For example,
+`chat` gets `/chat/completions` and `responses` gets `/responses`. The model
+list uses `/models` on the chat base, or the Responses base if chat is absent.
+The first matching model prefix selects its upstream protocol. The gateway
+still translates requests and replies. Keep one credential per private file;
+this adapter does not implement HMAC or a second account pool.
+
+`private_config.go` owns validation, request signing and direct transport.
+Redirects are returned without following them. A failed transport does not
+expose its private URL in the error. Files are read on each signing attempt,
+so credential rotation does not require a restart. Model refresh uses the same
+authentication and catalog pagination; excluded models are removed before saving.
+
+`private_errors.go` optionally normalizes wrapped HTTP/SSE error objects and
+turns an unfinished Responses stream into an explicit failure. This adapter
+does not retry, buffer whole generations or execute tools. The existing gateway
+owns retries, cooldowns, output commitment, cancellation and route tracing.
+The numeric status of a normalized SSE error participates in that classification.
+The adapter supports Bearer authentication only; do not point it at another
+authentication scheme or assume a server-side search bridge is provided.
+
+Verification: `TestPrivate*` in `internal/provider` and `internal/gateway`
+covers private serialization, permissions, redirects, cancellation, model
+pagination, credential rotation, wrapped errors and the replay boundary.
